{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/858695-2ed-mobile-freeholds","id":858695,"title":"[2ED] Mobile Freeholds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-03T19:56:22-07:00","id":858695,"title":"[2ED] Mobile Freeholds?","content":"I was taking another look at the Court Creation system. Let me state for the record that this is one of my favorite parts in all of CoD. But what might change about a Freehold whose great majority of members are regularly on the move? Could they let members of other Freeholds join to make up for those that decide to stay or went missing? Wouldn't that make the maintenance of the Bulwark more difficult? On the plus side, they could get inside a Mobile Hollow, ride Fae Mounts, use teleportation Tokens or another magical transportation.<br /> <br /> My guess is that the Stories at the center of each Court would become more fairy tale-like in their vagueness, or grow into a mythos that combines the tales of different nations across the eras. Approaches would include chases through the Ironside and the Hedge, and find-the-hidden-flag sort of challenges. The Huntsmen that go after these changelings would have their hands full.<br /> <br /> How would you write such a Freehold? Do you know any real life examples of nomadic groups that might work as inspiration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T20:18:21-07:00","id":858717,"title":"","content":"I think a mobile freehold is absolutely viable under the new system! There are plenty of nomadic groups throughout history! I think that an online freehold could be at thing too- think an MMO raiding guild or something though how it's structured would have to be done carefully but I've got a few ideas I'm chewing on in that department.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:05:14-07:00","id":859200,"title":"","content":"Not a mobile Freehold, but I had an idea for transity courts, Nomadic Courts that move from Freehold to Freehold, the court or courts temperarily adding themselves to the local court system, then removing their court from the Freehold when its time to move on.<br /> <br /> Example the Dawn Court and the Dusk Court. <br /> <br /> When the Prophets of the Dawn Court sense a time of prosperity and opportunity is coming for a Freehold, they members of one of its tribes make its way to that Freehold and add the Dawn Court to its preexisting court structure.<br /> <br /> This is seen by local Changeling Courts as a good omen, for prosperity and opportunity always comes with the Dawn Court.<br /> <br /> The Prophets of the Dusk Court on the other hand, seek out Freehold on the cusp of unusual danger, doom, or under terrorifying threats. While far from a good omen, the Dusk Court's fatalistic courage has won them grudging respect and in what is seen as ironic, has manage to save several Freeholds, although the Dusk Court sees it as but, a temperarily if welcome victory.<br /> <br /> In times of great risk and uncertainty, both the Dawn and Dusk Court can be attracted to the same Freehold at the same time. Its said to be a sign of interesting times ahead, filled both with dangers and potential rewards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:33:30-07:00","id":859253,"title":"","content":"I am working (slowly) on a completely nomadic freehold. They will be telling the story of the great american road trip. The Bulwark ritual I am working on will actually require travel in order to enact (currently thinking one group or individual must do a slideshow of new sites/sights while others play the bored family).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T15:39:10-07:00","id":859296,"title":"","content":"Interesting ideas here. It's also gotten me to thinking of what would a freehold be like if they were based on <i>mobility</i> itself, rather than a moving freehold - that is, courts based on transit, such as trains, buses, taxis or boats? The courts could take staff positions in the various services they run, themselves constantly be moving even while they set up a niche for themselves in their positions, and they each get their own sort of territory marked out by what routes they have access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T18:02:27-07:00","id":859356,"title":"","content":"One of the writers, I forget who, made a Court of the Road, and one of the Dark Eras make mention of Pirate Freeholds, or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T19:43:16-07:00","id":859398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/858695-2ed-mobile-freeholds?p=859356#post859356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the writers, I forget who, made a Court of the Road, and one of the Dark Eras make mention of Pirate Freeholds, or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe their username was eburg?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T19:50:46-07:00","id":859406,"title":"","content":"Yes, it was Eburg. I actually really liked that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T23:41:00-07:00","id":859493,"title":"","content":"Was that the circus Freehold, the one with a Court of the Road and a Court of the Ring?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T03:10:01-07:00","id":859534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/858695-2ed-mobile-freeholds?p=859356#post859356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the writers, I forget who, made a Court of the Road, and one of the Dark Eras make mention of Pirate Freeholds, or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a write-up on this somewhere? Pardon me for asking.<br /> <br /> On the subject of mobile freeholds, I'm wondering, now, if there exists a freehold system built upon the stories and beliefs of the various Roma (and Doma) groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T05:43:54-07:00","id":859569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a write-up on this somewhere? Pardon me for asking.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_NDcEF6Bn93LTlHZmxNN29EOVk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_N...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:17:05-07:00","id":859765,"title":"","content":"I think a mobile freehold would be a great idea. Considering a static location in the long run would make it more likley privateers, loyalists or a Gentry hunting party to show up, being mobile would be a great idea. <br /> <br /> Trains as mentioned would be a great idea. In modern time they'd be a little more difficult in terms of economics. You might have to have your cars attached to amtrax or freight trains. However during the industrial revolution Changelings could operate a passenger train quite easily all over the developed world. Whose to say that the Autumn Court isn't running the Orient Express and that's why weird occult things seem keep happening on it? <br /> <br /> As far as boats..pirate ships anyone? You could have a cargo ship that bounces around the south pacific islands. Or a smaller cruise ship that takes vacationers around the Mediterraian and the crew are all changelings. <br /> <br /> Heck, biker gangs could with small trailers attached to trikes could be a mobile freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:33:13-07:00","id":859880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/858695-2ed-mobile-freeholds?p=859569#post859569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_NDcEF6Bn93LTlHZmxNN29EOVk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_N...ew?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I love the Court and the contracts within, I'm a little disappointed because I thought we finally had an example of a Goblin Vow. XD Oh well, maybe later. For now, that's a really cool court, and I like that the initial contracts don't require a membership with the Court to take, even if the others do require some form of contact with them. Shame that the contracts don't have Seeming bonuses yet though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-05-2016, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}